  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "What a Pipeline Actually Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stage Array",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A pipeline is an ordered array of stage documents. Each stage takes a stream of documents in and emits a stream out, feeding the next."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "db.orders.aggregate([",
            "  { $match: { status: 'A' } },   // stage 1",
            "  { $group: { _id: '$region',",
            "      total: { $sum: '$amount' } } }",
            "], { allowDiskUse: true })"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every stage is one key: `{ $stageName: <spec> }`",
            "Two keys errors: 'must contain exactly one field'",
            "Same stage may repeat — `$match` before and after `$group`",
            "Not set operations; streaming transforms"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "collection",
              "$match",
              "$unwind",
              "$group",
              "$sort",
              "cursor"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stream Not Sets",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Input to stage 1 = whole collection or an index scan",
            "Input to stage N = output of N-1, never the collection",
            "Docs are plain BSON, need not match stored schema",
            "After `$group` the shape is whatever you built"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Against find()",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Job",
            "find()",
            "aggregate()"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "filter, sort, limit",
              "yes",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "group, facet",
              "no",
              "$group, $facet"
            ],
            [
              "join",
              "no",
              "$lookup"
            ],
            [
              "flatten array",
              "no",
              "$unwind"
            ],
            [
              "computed fields",
              "no",
              "$project"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`mapReduce` deprecated since 5.0 — replaced by aggregation",
            "Aggregation runs native C++, not a JS interpreter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Shell pipe model",
          "text": "`grep | sort | uniq -c` is exactly `$match | $sort | $group`. Same laziness, same ordering discipline."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            " {$group:{_id:'$p.category',",
            "   revenue:{$sum:{$multiply:",
            "     ['$items.qty','$items.price']}}}},",
            " {$sort:{revenue:-1}}, {$limit:10}]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Takes the find() query language whole: `$and`, `$or`, `$in`",
            "`$regex`, `$exists`, `$type` all valid here",
            "No aggregation expressions without `$expr`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Blocking Stages, Memory Caps & Filters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Streaming vs Blocking",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Class",
            "Stages"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "streaming",
              "$match, $project, $unwind"
            ],
            [
              "streaming",
              "$limit, $skip, $addFields"
            ],
            [
              "blocking",
              "$group, $sort, $bucket"
            ],
            [
              "blocking",
              "$facet, $setWindowFields"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cursor And Caps",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`aggregate()` returns a cursor — nothing runs until iterated",
            "16 MB cap is per document in and out, not per result set",
            "Result set streams through the cursor, any size",
            "100 MB per blocking stage: 'Exceeded memory limit for $group'",
            "`allowDiskUse: true` spills; default spill for $sort/$group 6.0+"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            " {$lookup:{from:'products',",
            "   localField:'items.sku',",
            "   foreignField:'sku', as:'p'}},",
            " {$unwind:{path:'$p',",
            "   preserveNullAndEmptyArrays:true}},"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Who orders stages",
          "items": [
            "You write the order; it is not yours to shuffle later",
            "The planner may reorder some stages for you",
            "Which ones, and when, in the optimizer chapter"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Filter Spec",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $match: {",
            "    status: 'A',",
            "    qty: { $gt: 10 },",
            "    tag: { $in: ['new','hot'] }",
            "} }   // same language as find()"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The whole handbook in one line",
          "text": "A `$match` at the very front can use an index. A `$match` after `$group`, `$unwind` or a reshaping `$project` usually cannot."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Indexes Die",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Indexes describe the stored collection, nothing else",
            "Once a stage invents fields, the stream is derived",
            "No index exists on a derived stream — full scan of it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "$match first",
                "lines": [
                  "IXSCAN on shipDate",
                  "10M docs to 5k",
                  "$group sees 5k"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "$match after $group",
                "lines": [
                  "COLLSCAN",
                  "10M docs grouped",
                  "filter every group"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Predicates, Regex & Cheap Counts",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two-Field Compares",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $match: { $expr: {",
            "  $gt: ['$qty', '$reorderLevel'] } } }",
            "// $expr needed: two fields, same doc",
            "// index use mostly lost here"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$expr` index support exists for `$eq`/`$lt`/`$gt` but is fragile",
            "Better: store a precomputed `belowReorder` flag at write time",
            "`$where` is banned in `$match`",
            "`$text` allowed only as the FIRST stage of the pipeline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Splitting Predicates",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Push filters early and narrow — 10M to 5k before `$group`",
            "That single move is three orders of magnitude of cost",
            "Index-friendly equality in stage 1; derived predicates later",
            "ESR: equality, then sort, then range picks the compound index"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// uses index on shipDate",
            "[{$match:{shipDate:{$gte:start}}},",
            " {$group:{_id:'$region',",
            "   total:{$sum:'$amount'}}}]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Shape",
            "Reads",
            "SQL kin"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "$match then $group",
              "index range",
              "WHERE"
            ],
            [
              "$group then $match",
              "every group",
              "HAVING"
            ],
            [
              "$match then $count",
              "index only",
              "COUNT(*)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Anchored Regex Only",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $match: { sku: /^AB/ } }",
            "// left-anchored: index prefix",
            "{ $match: { sku: /AB/ } }",
            "// unanchored: every key examined"
          ],
          "note": "only /^abc/ narrows the index"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only ==left-anchored== `/^abc/` can use an index prefix",
            "Unanchored patterns walk every index key or document",
            "Case-insensitive `/i` also loses the tight prefix bound"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Counting Cheaply",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "[{ $match: { status: 'paid' } },",
            " { $count: 'n' }]",
            "// -> { n: 4210 }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Count on the server; never pull docs to count them",
            "`$count` is sugar for `$group` then `$project`",
            "A leading indexed `$match` keeps it index-only"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Reading explain(): IXSCAN vs COLLSCAN",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Check The Gate",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`winningPlan`: ==IXSCAN== good, **COLLSCAN** means no index",
            "Healthy: `totalDocsExamined` ≈ `nReturned`",
            "1000:1 ratio means the leading `$match` missed its index",
            "`hint: 'idx_name'` forces an index when the planner picks badly"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "$group Shape & Accumulators",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Small print",
          "items": [
            "`{ $match: {} }` is legal, a no-op, and blocks stage merging — delete it",
            "`$count: 'n'` is sugar for `$group` plus `$project`",
            "`{ field: null }` also matches docs where the field is missing",
            "Mean present? `{ field: { $ne: null, $exists: true } }`"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Group Shape",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $group: {",
            "  _id: '$region',        // mandatory",
            "  total: { $sum: '$amount' },",
            "  n: { $sum: 1 }         // row counter",
            "} }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`_id: null` puts every doc in one bucket — the grand total",
            "`_id` may be a document for a composite key",
            "`_id: { region: '$region', year: { $year: '$date' } }`",
            "Output `_id` is then that subdocument"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Accumulator Set",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Accumulator",
            "Gives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "$sum, $avg",
              "totals, means"
            ],
            [
              "$min, $max",
              "extremes"
            ],
            [
              "$first, $last",
              "needs prior $sort"
            ],
            [
              "$push, $addToSet",
              "array, deduped array"
            ],
            [
              "$stdDevPop/Samp",
              "spread"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$mergeObjects` folds subdocuments together",
            "`$top`/`$bottom`/`$topN`/`$bottomN` since 5.2",
            "`$sum: 1` is idiomatic; `$count: {}` is the 5.0+ equivalent",
            "Without a `$sort`, `$first`/`$last` are undefined order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $group: { _id: '$region',",
            "  top3: { $topN: { n: 3,",
            "    sortBy: { amount: -1 },",
            "    output: '$amount' } } } }"
          ],
          "note": "bounded, unlike $push"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost Is Distinct Count",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "EU",
              "US",
              "APAC",
              "LATAM",
              "...",
              "80M?"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "buffered groups"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blocking: no output until the last input doc is consumed",
            "Memory is proportional to distinct groups, not input docs",
            "100M docs by day = 365 groups = cheap",
            "Same 100M by `userId` = 80M groups = not cheap",
            "`$push`/`$addToSet` are unbounded — 16 MB doc cap looms"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Push only what you need",
          "text": "`$push: '$sku'`, not `$push: '$$ROOT'`. Whole documents in one group hit ==BSONObjectTooLarge== fast; `$topN` caps the array."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Why $group Drops Your Fields",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Destructive by design",
          "text": "Anything not in `_id` and not an accumulator is dropped. `$group` is where your schema disappears."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "HAVING, $project & $addFields",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shorthands And HAVING",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$sortByCount: '$tag'` = group by tag, `$sum:1`, sort desc",
            "Post-group `$match` is SQL's HAVING clause",
            "`{ $group } , { $match: { total: { $gte: 100 } } }`",
            "DISTINCT_SCAN: group on an index's leading field with only `$first`/`$last` can skip-scan"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "[{$match:{status:'paid'}},",
            " {$group:{_id:'$custId',",
            "   total:{$sum:'$amount'}}},",
            " {$sort:{total:-1}}, {$limit:5}]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Silent skew",
          "items": [
            "`$avg` and `$sum` ignore non-numeric values, no error",
            "A stored `'42'` string contributes nothing at all",
            "Average drops because the count differs from what you assume"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Include Or Exclude",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`{ a: 1, b: 1 }` keeps only `a`, `b` and `_id`",
            "`{ a: 0 }` drops `a`, keeps everything else",
            "Mixing the two errors — one exception below",
            "`_id: 0` may join an inclusion projection",
            "`_id` is the only field you must exclude by hand"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $project: {",
            "  _id: 0, sku: 1,",
            "  total: { $multiply:",
            "    ['$price', '$qty'] }   // computed",
            "} }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Add Without Shrinking",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $addFields: { line: '$price' } }",
            "{ $set: { line: '$price' } }  // alias, 4.2+",
            "{ $unset: ['tmp', 'debug.trace'] }",
            "{ $replaceWith: '$profile' }  // promote sub"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$addFields` adds or overwrites, keeps the rest",
            "Use it whenever you are not trying to shrink the doc",
            "`$unset` is an alias for exclusion projection",
            "`$replaceRoot`/`$replaceWith` lifts a subdocument to top level"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Paths And Literals",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Field paths carry a leading dollar: `'$price'`",
            "A real string starting with `$` needs `{ $literal: '$price' }`",
            "Dotted paths reach into subdocuments",
            "`'$items.sku'` over an array yields an array of skus"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Family",
            "Operators"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "branching",
              "$cond, $ifNull, $switch"
