    },
    {
      "page_title": "Projection Cost & $unwind Basics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shrink Before Blocking",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Projecting to a few fields before `$sort`/`$group` cuts buffered bytes",
            "Real win on wide documents, measurable in explain",
            "Covered pipeline: leading `$match` plus `$project` touching only indexed fields",
            "Covered means zero document fetches — requires `_id: 0`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Three traps",
          "items": [
            "A giant early `$project` renaming everything destroys index-eligible names downstream",
            "Projecting a missing field creates nothing — not null, just absent",
            "`$addFields` never blocks, but bigger docs cost the next `$sort`/`$group` memory"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Doc Per Element",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $unwind: '$items' }   // short form",
            "{ $unwind: { path: '$items',",
            "    includeArrayIndex: 'idx',",
            "    preserveNullAndEmptyArrays: true } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "items[0]",
              "items[1]",
              "items[2]"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "1 doc, items[3] becomes 3 docs"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The array field is replaced by that single element",
            "Fan-out: N docs with 10-element arrays become 10N docs",
            "This is where pipelines go quadratic",
            "`includeArrayIndex` records the zero-based position",
            "A non-array scalar passes through as a one-element array"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Silent data loss",
          "text": "By default `$unwind` DROPS docs where the field is missing, null or `[]`. Set `preserveNullAndEmptyArrays: true` whenever a missing array is meaningful."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Input Cases",
          "ink": "green"
