    {
      "page_title": "Fan-Out Costs & $lookup Joins",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Nested double `$unwind` multiplies: 10 inside 10 gives 100 per doc",
            "Since 3.2 the planner may push a following `$match` back before it",
            "Only when the predicate is independent of the unwound path",
            "`$unwind` cannot use an index — index use must come earlier"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "No-Fan-Out Alternatives",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "In-place operator"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "keep some elements",
              "$filter"
            ],
            [
              "transform each",
              "$map"
            ],
            [
              "fold to one value",
              "$reduce, $sum"
            ],
            [
              "length",
              "$size"
            ],
            [
              "one element",
              "$arrayElemAt"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost And Rebuild",
          "ink": "black"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`$unwind` itself is streaming and cheap per document",
            "The cost lands on the next blocking `$group` or `$sort`",
            "Classic pattern: unwind, then group back per element",
            "Revenue per line-item SKU across orders is exactly that"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "[{$unwind:'$tags'},",
            " {$sortByCount:'$tags'}]   // histogram",
            "// rebuild the array afterwards:",
            "{$group:{_id:'$_id',",
            "  items:{$push:'$items'}}}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Left Outer Join",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $lookup: {",
            "  from: 'items',",
            "  localField: 'sku',",
            "  foreignField: 'sku',",
            "  as: 'itemDocs' } }   // always an array"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`as` holds matched docs, `[]` when nothing matched",
            "Almost always followed by `$unwind` or `$arrayElemAt`",
            "The local side gets no index help for the join itself",
            "So filter the local side with a leading `$match` first"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Index the foreign field",
          "text": "Without an index on `foreignField`, MongoDB runs a collection scan per input document — an O(N x M) nested loop."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pipeline Form",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "{ $lookup: { from: 'lines',",
            "  let: { id: '$_id' },",
            "  pipeline: [{ $match: { $expr:",
            "    { $eq: ['$orderId','$$id'] } } },",
            "    { $limit: 50 }], as: 'x' } }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Outer fields must be bound in `let`, read as `$$id`",
            "A plain `'$field'` inside refers to the FOREIGN document",
            "Available since 3.6; lets you filter and project the joined side",
            "5.0+ allows `localField`/`foreignField` AND a pipeline together"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
